  * CPM gating, AFR, the non-CPU SoC clusters and SIO are shared with s2idle
  * and live in apple-sleep.
+ *
+ * T8132 (M4) has no CPU complex sequence that is known to work. With the
+ * t8132_sequence parameter set at boot, ->enter instead follows the order
+ * macOS uses on that SoC, as Aurora measured and ported it: AP wake masks,
+ * macOS's power words, the parked CPUs stopped, then IO, memory controller,
+ * gates, CPU clusters, clock muxes and the PMGR commit, and on the wake the
+ * clusters, gates and power words back and the SEP's DEV_DISABLE cleared.
+ * The boot CPU, the warm boot mailbox, the coprocessor stops, the breadcrumb,
+ * the bring-up watchdog and abort_before are this driver's, as above.
  */
 
 #include <linux/bitfield.h>
